Slice 3 of the falsifiable-packet bet (FPK-V0-012). `prove --cem MAP
--expected-base REV --target REV` runs the frozen CEM verifier exactly as
`cem verify` does, embeds that document unchanged, and emits one row per
hunk. Supported and mechanical hunks get `verifier-accepts`; explicit
unknowns get `none`. A row passes only when the verifier accepted the whole
map and the hunk's basis evidence is stable or relocated at the target; a
rejected map fails every claim row and reports state REJECTED. Missing
verifier inputs stay typed exit-2 failures rather than verdicts.

